  "network": "Separate server/client processes on clean IPv4 loopback, transparent counting proxy in client process; no artificial bandwidth/latency/loss.",
  "counters": "Successfully forwarded TCP stream bytes / UDP datagram bytes, both directions exactly once; includes handshake, dictionary updates/ACKs, application receipts and reliable transport controls/retries; excludes IP/transport/link headers and final harness shutdown message.",
  "phases": "See per-workload phasePlans. Standard workloads use cold64, warm128, stop-and-wait latency64. adaptive-32k uses fresh random64, repeated64, fresh random churn64, return of original64, byte-runs64, stop-and-wait byte-runs latency64; one cache persists across phases. spaced-32k repeats a cycle of32 independently seeded random objects, using the standard phases. Bulk RTT uses window8. Byte snapshots include trailing controls after160ms quiet and a reliable-UDP server queue-drain barrier (included in bytes); settling is excluded from throughput timers. Setup timing is Connect only; setup byte counts include its quiet drain.",
